                            </owl:Class>
                        </owl:someValuesFrom>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <obo:definition>Modified apical cell, having a thickened or enlarged morphology.  Has a hood-like, lid-like, or cap-like form.  Little is known about the role, although presence is environmentally influenced.  Not all trichomes in a natural population will exhibit a calyptra.  Found in the Oscillatoriales and Nostocales.

</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>end cells aways with calyptra</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://huey.colorado.edu/cyanobacteria/taxa/calyptra.php

Definition of Calyptra

Thickened or enlarged tip of a cyanobacterial filament, a hoodlike, lidlike, or caplike structure.</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


