        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Zobell phytagel starch agar</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, mineral-salts, liquid microbiological culture medium containing peptones and yeast extract in a base of artificial sea water.  Solidified using Phytagel instead of agar.  Supplemented with starch.  Used for the cultivation of heterotrophic marine microorganisms capable of degrading agar.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Barbeyron T, L&apos;Haridon S, Corre E, Kloareg B &amp; Potin P.  2001.  Zobellia galactanovorans gen. nov., sp. nov., a marine species of Flavobacteriaceae isolated from a red alga, and classification of [Cytophaga] uliginosa (ZoBell and Upham 1944) Reichenbach 1989 as Zobellia uliginosa gen. nov., comb. nov.  IJSEM 51:985-997.

