        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-proline 4-nitroanilide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>L-proline arylamidase that uses the substrate L-proline 4-nitroanilide (L-proline-p-nitroanilide).  Proline arylamidase activity (which could be from proline aminopeptidase as well as other dipeptidase enzymes) cleaves the substrate, releasing 4-nitroaniline which is bright yellow in color.

A positive test is yellow; a negative test is colorless.</obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Proline p-nitroanilide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>PRO</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-proline-p-nitroanilide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


