        <obo:has_exact_synonym>methanogens</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>formation of CH4</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>production of CH4</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>CH4 generated</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>methane formation</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:methanogenesis

Methanogenesis or biomethanation is the formation of methane by microbes known as methanogens.  Organisms capable of producing methane have been identified only from the domain Archaea, a group phylogenetically distinct from both eukaryotes and bacteria, although many live in close association with anaerobic bacteria.  The production of methane is an important and widespread form of microbial metabolism. In most environments, it is the final step in the decomposition of biomass.</obo:IAO_0000119>
