        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>manure extract</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <obo:definition>A water extract of horse (Equus caballus) manure, used for the culturing of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From &quot;Report of the New York State College of Agriculture at Cornell University, Ithaca, and of the Cornell University Agricultural Experiment Station&quot;, v. 25, Part 1, 1913, pg. 431:

Manure extract agar. - Prepared as follows: To 100 grams of well-rotted horse manure was added 500 cc. of distilled water.  This was allowed to stand for twenty-four hours at room temperature and then filtered.  The filtrate was used as a stock solution.
</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


