    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MICRO_0000264 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0000264">
        <rdfs:label>diazocyte</rdfs:label>
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0000527"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;BFO_0000050"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;NCBITaxon_1205"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000280"/>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic differentiated cell capable of nitrogen fixation, found in Trichodesmium species (Cyanobacteria).  Diazocytes are mostly found in the center cells of Trichodesmium filaments.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From Sandh, Xu &amp; Bergman, 2012, Diazocyte development in the marine diazotrophic cyanobacterium Trichodesmium.  Microbiology 158:345-352.:

The establishment of non-diazotrophic cultures of the filamentous marine cyanobacterium Trichodesmium erythraeum IMS101 enabled the first detailed investigation of the process leading to the development of its unique nitrogen-fixing cell type, the diazocyte.</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


