        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://microbeonline.com/bacterial-flagella-structure-importance-and-examples-of-flagellated-bacteria/

Amphitrichous: Single flagellum at both ends e.g. Alcaligenes faecalis  (Mneomonics: Remember: the characteristics of Amphibians: live both in land and water) </obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


