                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <obo:definition>Uses the substrate N-benzoyl-D-L-arginine 2-naphthylamide at pH 8.5.  Trypsin activity will cleave the substrate, releasing 2-naphthylamide.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate that is orange in color.</obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>N-benzoyl-arginine-2-naphthylamide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>N-benzoyl-DL-arginine-2-naphthylamide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


