        <dc:source>Fallon RJ.  1967.  Mycoplasmas and their role as rodent pathogens.  Lab Anim 1:43.  DOI: 10.1258/002367767781006794.</dc:source>
        <obo:definition>A colony having distinct physical quality that is shaped like a mulberry (acinar), sunken, and opaque with little or no pale periphery.  Is typical of young colonies of Mycoplasma species that will develop into colonies that have a fried egg appearance when more mature.</obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>mulberry</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


