        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:Vibrio

Vibrio is a genus of Gram-negative bacteria possessing a curved rod shape (comma shape), several species of which can cause foodborne infection, usually associated with eating undercooked seafood.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic cell, being a bacillus where the elongated axis of the cells is curved (but not spiral).</obo:definition>
