                                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;NCBITaxon_1129"/>
                                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;NCBITaxon_1218"/>
                                </owl:unionOf>
                            </owl:Class>
                        </owl:someValuesFrom>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <obo:definition>Prokaryotes or single-celled eukaryotes that have a cell size between 0.2 and 2 micrometers in diameter, that are photosynthetic (use light as a source of energy), and that are members of the genus Prochlorococcus and iin some members of the genus Synechococcus (both Cyanobacteria).</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: Scanlan DJ et al.  2009.  Ecological genomics of marine picocyanobacteria.  Microbiol Mol Biol Rev 73(2):249-299.

Marine picocyanobacteria of the genera Prochlorococcus and Synechococcus numerically dominate the picophytoplankton of the world ocean, making a key contribution to global primary production.</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


