        <obo:definition>A microbiological assay of lysis of blood cells, where the assay is for cytolysis of red blood cells.  Hemolysis assays are carried out using some formulation of blood agar, and the assay involves determination of whether lysis has occured and the nature of the lysis.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
