        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: Staley JT.  1981.  The genera Prosthecomicrobium and Ancalomicrobium. In: Starr MP, Stolp H, Truper HG, Balows A,Schlegel HG, (eds). The prokaryotes. Berlin: Springer-Verlag.  Pg 68.

Vitamin Solution

B12              0.1 mg
Biotin           2 mg
Calcium pantothenate        5 mg
Folic acid              2 mg
nicotinamide        5 mg
pyridoxine HCl      10 mg
riboflavin     5 mg
thiamine HCL       5 mg
Add distilled water up to 1 L and store in 4˚C in a dark container.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>A solution of B vitamins including cobalamin (B12), biotin (B7), pantothenic acid (B5), folic acid (B9), nicotinamide (B3), pyridoxine (B6), riboflavin (B2), and thiamine (B1).  Used to support the growth of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


