                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:intersectionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>urease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>URE</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>urea hydrolysis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>urease test</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <obo:definition>An enzymatic assay which tests for the presence of urease in a microorganism.  Urease hydrolyzes urea to produce CO2 and ammonia, which increases the pH of the media:

(NH2)2CO + H2O -&gt; CO2 + 2 NH3

The urease test uses phenol red as a pH indicator.  An increase in alkalinity results in a color from yellow to pink/red.

A positive result is pink/orange/red; a negative test result is yellow.

The test employs either Christensen&apos;s Urea Agar or Stuart&apos;s Urea Broth.</obo:definition>
        <obo:database_cross_reference>http://www.microbelibrary.org/library/laboratory-test/3223-urease-test-protocol</obo:database_cross_reference>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


