                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001458"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001494"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:Chemotroph

Chemotrophs are organisms that obtain energy by the oxidation of electron donors in their environments.  These molecules can be organic (chemoorganotrophs) or inorganic (chemolithotrophs).  The chemotroph designation is in contrast to phototrophs, which utilize solar energy.  Chemotrophs can be either autotrophic or heterotrophic.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic respiratory metabolic process where the oxidation and reduction of chemical compounds is the energy source.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank
</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


