        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic respiratory metabolic process where light is the energy source.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:Phototroph

Phototrophs are the organisms that carry out photon capture to acquire energy.  They use the energy from light to carry out various cellular metabolic processes.  Most of the well-recognized phototrophs are autotrophs, also known as photoautotrophs, and can fix carbon.  </obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MICRO_0000499 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0000499">
