        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001504"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic respiratory metabolic process where the oxidation and reduction of chemical compounds is the energy source, and the electron donor is an organic compound.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:Primary nutritional groups

Chemoorganotrophs are organisms which oxidize the chemical bonds in organic compounds as their energy source. Chemoorganotrophs also attain the carbon molecules that they need for cellular function from these organic compounds. The organic compounds that they oxidize include sugars (i.e. glucose), fats and proteins).[2]</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


