        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic respiratory metabolic process where light is the energy source, and the electron donor is an organic compound.</obo:definition>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>photoheterotroph</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:Photoheterotroph

Photoheterotrophs are heterotrophic organisms that use light for energy, but cannot use carbon dioxide as their sole carbon source. Consequently, they use organic compounds from the environment to satisfy their carbon requirements; these compounds include carbohydrates, fatty acids, and alcohols. Examples of photoheterotrophic organisms include purple non-sulfur bacteria, green non-sulfur bacteria, and heliobacteria.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank
</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


