                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001478"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>Wikipedia:Microbial metabolism


Chemolithoheterotrophs obtain energy from the oxidation of inorganic compounds, but cannot fix carbon dioxide (CO2). Examples: some Thiobacillus, some Beggiatoa, some Nitrobacter spp., Wolinella (with H2 as reducing equivalent donor), some Knallgas-bacteria, some sulfate-reducing bacteria.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic respiratory metabolic process where the oxidation and reduction of chemical compounds is the energy source, the electron donor is an inorganic compound, and the carbon source is an organic compound.</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


