        <obo:IAO_0000119>Humphry DR, George A, Black GW &amp; Cummings SP.  2001.  Flavobacteirum frigidarium sp. nov., an aerobic, psychrophilic, xylanolytic and laminariolytic bacterium from Antarctica.  IJSEM 51:1235-1243.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium246.pdf

DSMZ Medium 246

246.  SEA WATER AGAR

Beef extract 10.0 g
Peptone 10.0 g
Agar 20.0 g
Tap water 250.0 ml
Sea water* 750.0 ml

Dissolve beef extract and peptone by heating in tap water, adjust pH to 7.8 and boil for 10 min. Readjust pH to 7.3. Add agar and autoclave at 121°C for 20 min. Directly after autoclaving, add warm (55°C) sterile sea water. Liquid medium without agar should be combined when cooled to room temperature.

*Natural sea water is stored in the dark for at least three weeks to &quot;age&quot;. If natural sea water is not available use artificial sea water.

Artificial sea water:
NaCl    28.13 g
KCl    0.77 g
CaCl2 x 2 H2O    1.60 g
MgCl2 x 6 H2O    4.80 g
NaHCO3    0.11 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O    3.50 g
Distilled water    1000.0 ml

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, marine, solid microbiological culture medium containing beef extract and peptone, in a diluted artificial sea water base.  Used for the growth of marine Flavobacterium.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


