        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: Peptone Water (Becton-Dickinson Difco and BBL Manual of Microbiological Culture Media, 2nd edition):

Intended Use
Peptone Water is used for cultivating nonfastidious organisms, for studying carbohydrate fermentation patterns and for performing the indole test.

Principles of the Procedure
Peptone Water contains peptone as a source of carbon, nitrogen, vitamins and minerals. Sodium chloride maintains the osmotic balance of the medium.

Formula
Difco™ Peptone Water
Approximate Formula* Per Liter
Peptone..................................................................... 10.0 g
Sodium Chloride.......................................................... 5.0 g
*Adjusted and/or supplemented as required to meet performance criteria.

pH 7.2 ± 0.2</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, liquid microbiological culture medium containing peptone and sodium chloride.  </obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>peptone water</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


