        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/laked+blood

laked blood
[lākt]
Etymology: Fr, laque, a deep red color
blood that is clear, red, and homogenous because of hemolysis of the red blood cells, as may occur in poisoning and severe extensive burns.
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>A solid microbiological culture medium (a blood agar), made with laked blood (where the red blood cells have been treated so that they have undergone haemolysis).</obo:definition>
