        <obo:has_exact_synonym>EG blood agar</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: Eggerth AH &amp; Gagnon BH.  1932.  The bacteroides of human feces.  J Bacteriol 35(4):389-413.

&quot;Our basic medium was beef infusion agar, containing 1.5 per cent of agar, 1 per cent of Parke Davis peptone, and 0.4 per cent of di-sodium phosphate.  The pH was 7.6 to 7.8.  Before pouring the plates, about 5 per cent of sterile blood and 0.15 per cent of sterile glucose (in the form of a 10 per cent solution) were added.&quot;</obo:IAO_0000119>
