    <owl:Class rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0000608">
        <rdfs:label>ox gall</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000610"/>
        <obo:definition>Gall (bile stored in the gall bladder) derived from an ox (a castrated adult male bovine; Bos taurus), used for the culturing of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From Wikipedia:Ox_gall:

Ox gall is gall, usually obtained from cows, that is mixed with alcohol and used as the wetting agent in paper marbling, engraving, lithography, and watercolor painting. It is a greenish-brown liquid mixture containing cholesterol, lecithin, taurocholic acid, and glycocholic acid.

</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Oxgall</obo:has_exact_synonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


