        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>Assays for the ability of an organism to break down the protein casein.  Usually tested by incorporating casein into agar.  A positive test will result in clearing of the agar due to degradation of the opaque casein.  Commonly uses Milk Agar or Casein Agar.</obo:definition>
        <rdfs:comment>has component some casein</rdfs:comment>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>casein hydrolysis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


