        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:database_cross_reference>Wikipedia:Gelatinase</obo:database_cross_reference>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>gelatin hydrolysis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>gelatinase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>GEL</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:definition>An assay for the presence of gelatinase in a microorganism.  Gelatinase is a proteolytic enzyme that breaks down gelatin (a partially hydrolyzed form of collagen derived from animal tissue that is comprised of peptides and proteins) via a hydrolysis reaction.  Gelatin hydrolysis (a positive reaction) is found when the liquefaction of a gelatin-containing substrate is observed.</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


