        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>N-acetyl-beta-glucosaminidase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>bNAG</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:definition>An assay for the activity of N-acetyl-beta-glucosaminidase in a microorganism.  Uses the substrate 1-naphthyl-N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminide at pH 5.4.  N-acetyl-beta-glucosaminidase activity (catalyzing the hydrolysis of terminal beta-N-acetylglucosamine residues from oligosaccharides) will cleave the substrate, producing 1-naphthol.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate (an azo dye) that is brown in color.</obo:definition>
        <rdfs:comment>zzzz

naphthol is not napthyl</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


