        <obo:definition>A carbohydrate hydrolysis assay for the activity of beta-mannosidase in a microorganism using the substrate 6-bromo-2-naphthyl-beta-D-mannopyranoside at pH 5.4.  beta-Mannosidase activity (catalyzing the hydrolysis of terminal non-reducing beta-D-mannose residues in beta-D-mannosides) will cleave the substrate, producing 6-bromo-2-naphthol.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate (a bromo substituted azo dye) that is purple in color.</obo:definition>
