        <obo:definition>An alpha-amino acid arylamidase assay that uses the substrate L-valyl-2-naphthylamide at pH 7.5.  Valine arylamidase activity (which could be from valine aminopeptidase as well as other dipeptidase enzymes) will cleave the substrate, releasing 2-naphthylamide.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate that is orange in color.

