        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>2-naphthyl-b-L-fucoside</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:definition>An assay for the activity of beta-L-fucosidase in a microorganism.  Uses the substrate 2-naphthyl-beta-L-fucoside at pH 5.4.  beta-Fusosidase activity (catalyzing the hydrolysis of terminal non-reducing beta-L-fucose residues in beta-fucosides) will cleave the substrate, producing 2-naphthol.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate (an azo dye) that is purple in color.</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


