        <obo:has_exact_synonym>ORN</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-orgnithine decarboxylase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>decarboxylations of the amino acid ornithine by ornithine decarboxylase (sic)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>ODC</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:database_cross_reference>Wikipedia:Ornithine_decarboxylase</obo:database_cross_reference>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ornithine carboxy-lyase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:definition>The purpose of this test is to determine if a microbial isolate is capable of metabolizing ornithine under anaerobic conditions.  When ornithine is metabolized, the pH of the medium increases due to the accumulation of ammonia and organic amines (e.g. putrescine).  This turns color of the pH indicator (e.g. bromcresol purple, cresol red) to red/orange.

A positive test yields a red/orange color; a negative test is yellow.

Ornithine decarboxylase catalyzes the reaction:
L-ornithine &lt;=&gt; putrescine + CO2</obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ornithine decarboxylase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


