        <obo:definition>Assays for the ability of a microorganism to ferment inulose (inulobiose).  Inulin is a fructooligosaccharide polymer, found in some plants, which often has a terminal glucose.  Glucose-free inulin is inulose.  Think it is more likely that it is a mistaken representation for inulobiose.</obo:definition>
