        <obo:definition>An assay for the activity of alpha-fucosidase in a microorganism.  Uses the substrate 2-naphthyl-alpha-L-fucopyranoside.  Alpha-fucosidase will cleave the substrate, producing 2-napthol.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate (an azo dye) that is purple in color.

A positive result is purple; a negative result is colorless.

</obo:definition>
