                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>OPS</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>NPPP</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>phenylphosphonate</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>phosphonate monoester hydrolase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>p-NP-phenyl-phosphonate</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>bis-p-nitrophenyl-phenyl-phosphonate</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>phosphonate hydrolase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:definition>Phosphonate hydrolase is an esterase that hydrolyzes a phosphonate compound (an organophosphorus compound with multiple alklyl or aryl groups).  p-nitrophenyl phenyl phosphonate is a substrate (NPPP) for phosphonate hydrolase enzymes.  Hydrolysis of this compound releases 4-nitrophenol (p-nitrophenol), which is yellow.  

A positive result is yellow; a negative result is colorless.</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


