        <obo:definition>As assay for the activity of phospholipase C (phosphorylcholine hydrolase); an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of the glycerophosphate bond of phospholipids.

Uses the substrate bis-p-nitrophenyl-phosphoryl-choline.  Phospholipase C will cleave the substrate, producing 4-nitrophenol which is yellow.  

A positive result is yellow; a negative result is colorless.</obo:definition>
