                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001198"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;CHEBI_88330"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001206"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001253"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-cysteine arylamidase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DL-cysteine-beta-naphthylamide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cysteine aminopeptidase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-cysteine aminopeptidase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-cysteine-b-naphthylamide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>L-cysteine-2-naphthylamide</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cysteine arylamidase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:definition>An alpha-amino acid arylamidase assay that uses the substrate L-cysteine-2-naphthylamide at pH 7.5.  Cysteine arylamidase activity (which could be from cysteine aminopeptidase as well as other dipeptidase enzymes) will cleave the substrate, releasing 2-naphthylamide.  When reacted with Fast Blue BB it forms a colored insoluble precipitate that is orange in color.

A positive reaction is orange; a negative reaction is colorless.
</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


