            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:definition>Assays for the ability of a microorganism to hydrolyze alpha-amino acid substrates coordinated with a beta-naphthylamide (2-naphthylamide) moiety.

Arylamidases are classes of enzymes with the ability to hydrolyze amino acid-beta-naphtylamide substrates.  Sheahan JP, Eitenmiller RR, &amp; Carpenter JA.  1975.  Arylamidase activity of Salmonella species.  Appl Microbiol 29(6):726-728.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


