                        </owl:intersectionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:definition>An enzymatic assay which tests for the presence of phosphogluconate dehydrogenase in a microorganism.  Phosphogluconate dehydrogenase (phosphogluconate 2-dehydrogenase, 6-phosphogluconic dehydrogenase, gluconate 6-phosphate dehydrogenase, 2-keto-6-phosphogluconate reductase) catalyzes the following reaction:

6-phospho-D-gluconate + NAD(P) &lt;=&gt; 6-phospho-2-dehydro-D-gluconate + NAD(P)H + H+</obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>phosphogluconate dehydrogenase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


