            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pyruvate decarboxylase</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:definition>An enzymatic assay which tests for the presence of pyruvate decarboxylase in a microorganism.  Pyruvate decarboxylase (also known as alpha-carboxylase, pyruvic decarboxylase, alpha-ketoacid carboxylase, 2-oxo-acid carboxy-lyase) catalyzes the following reactions:

a 2-oxo acid &lt;=&gt; an aldehyde + CO2
Pyruvate &lt;=&gt; acetaldehyde + CO2
Pyruvate + thiamine diphosphate &lt;=&gt; 2-(alpha-hydroxyethyl)thiamine diphosphate + CO2
Acetaldehde + thiamine diphosphate &lt;=&gt; 2-(alpha-hydroxyethyl)thiamine diphosphate</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


