        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:database_cross_reference>EC:1.97.1.-</obo:database_cross_reference>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>TRD</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>TET</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:definition>An assay for the presence of tetrathionate reductase in a microorganism.  Tetrathionate reductase carries out the following set of reactions:

tetrathionate + a reduced electron acceptor &lt;=&gt; 2 thiosulfate + an oxidized electron acceptor

Tetrationate reduction generates acid, and therefore the pH drops.  Some tests look for acid production in the presence of tetrathionate.</obo:definition>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>aliphatic thiol</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


