    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MICRO_0001172 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0001172">
        <rdfs:label>CAMP assay</rdfs:label>
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0000450"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000001"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000114"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001433"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom>
                            <owl:Class>
                                <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;NCBITaxon_1280"/>
                                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;NCBITaxon_1301"/>
                                </owl:unionOf>
                            </owl:Class>
                        </owl:someValuesFrom>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000450"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000001"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0000114"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="&obo;MICRO_0001433"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;NCBITaxon_1280"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;NCBITaxon_1301"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.microbelibrary.org/component/resource/laboratory-test/3086-camp-test-protocols</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>A beta-hemolysis assay used to identify Streptococcus agalactiae (Group B) and to differentiate it from Streptococcus pyrogenes (Group A) and other (Group C to Group H) streptococci.  

Group B streptococci are CAMP positive; Group A and Nongroup B streptococci are CAMP negative.

The assay is performed on Trypticase Soy Agar plates with sheep blood.  

The test/unknown Streptococcus organism is streaked onto TSA plates at right angles to the beta-lysin positive Staphycoccus aureus.  In a positive test (CAMP +) outcome, enhanced zones of clearing will be seen around the test organism when it is near the Staph. aureus.  This means that there is a synergistic respones between the test organism and the beta-lysin secreted by the Staph. aureus.  In a negative test (CAMP - ) outcome, no enhanced zone of clearing will be seen.

</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MICRO_0001173 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0001173">
        <rdfs:label>indole nitrate medium</rdfs:label>
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="&obo;MICRO_0000067"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
