        <obo:definition>A microbiological diagnostic assay for the ability of a microbial colony to develop an irridescent film when grown on egg yolk agar.  The irridescence is due to the presence of lipase, which causes the breakdown of fats (triglycerides into free fatty acids) in the egg yolk.</obo:definition>
