        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spots</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spot reaction</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:definition>An assay for the ability of a microbial colony to develop crystalline spots, or a fine crystalline deposit, when grown on egg yolk agar.  The spots are due to precipitation of calcium and magnesium &quot;soaps&quot; that are usually associated with a positive film reaction (i.e. the relase of fatty acid anions by lipolytic activity that combine with free calcium and magnesium in the medium).
</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


