            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>A Berkefeld filter assay that tests whether a prokaryotic cell is small enough to pass through a Berkefeld filter candle with a narrow pore size V (for Viel).  Pore sizes average 0.38 microns in diameter.  This is the most common filter size used to study the filterability of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


