        <obo:definition>An aqueous (water) extract of the dried liver of a mammal (typically a cow), used in the cultivation of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>liver infusion</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=13

To prepare liver extract, put 10 g liver powder in 170 ml water, keep at 50 to 60C for 1 hr, boil for 5 min, adjust pH to 7.2 and filter. </obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


