        <obo:definition>A prokaryotic metabolic process where the carbon or energy sources are organic compounds.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: Worden AZ, Follows MJ, Giovannoni SJ, Wilken S, Zimmerman AE, Keeling PJ.  2015.  Rethinking the marine carbon cycle: Factoring in the multifarious lifestyles of microbes.  Science 347, DOI: 10.1126/science.1257594.

(ii) Osmotrophy: Cells take up organic material from the external environment as small molecules or macromolecules.</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>osmotrophy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
