            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:definition>Blood medium ingredient comprised of a peptic digest of sheep (Ovis aries) or horse (Equus caballus) blood, serves as a source of hemin and NAD (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide).  Used in the cultivation of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: https://catalog.hardydiagnostics.com/cp_prod/Content/hugo/AnimalBloodProd.htm

Fildes Enrichment is a peptic digest of sheep or horse blood that serves as a rich source of growth factors including hemin (X-factor) and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide (V-factor).</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


