        <obo:definition>Blood medium ingredient comprised of horse (Equus caballus) blood where heparin has been added to prevent coagulation.  Used in the cultivation of microorganisms.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>From: https://catalog.hardydiagnostics.com/cp_prod/Content/hugo/AnimalBloodProd.htm

Horse Blood, with Heparin is whole horse blood treated with the anticoagulant heparin. Heparin-binding of Mycobacterium tuberculosis has been suggested to increase the organism&apos;s virulence in primary infection and in extrapulmonary dissemination(5). </obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


