        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, liquid culture medium containing sea salts, ammonium chloride, peptone, yeast extract, riboflavin, and glucose.  Used for the cultivation of Maricaulis.</obo:definition>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Maricaulis medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1025.pdf

1025. MARICAULIS MEDIUM

Sigma Sea salts 30.0 g
NH4Cl 0.5 g
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

Autoclave and cool the medium. Add from sterile stock solutions, 20 ml 50xPYE and 5 ml 0.2 mg/ml riboflavin (filter sterilised), and 2 ml 50% glucose per liter of medium.

50xPYE:
Peptone 100.0 g
Yeast extract 50.0 g
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


