        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Thiomonas intermedia medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>DSM strains:
</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium35a.pdf

35a. THIOMONAS INTERMEDIA MEDIUM

NH4Cl 0.1 g
KH2PO4 3.0 g
MgCl2 x 6 H2O 0.1 g
CaCl2 0.1 g
Na2S2O3 x 5 H2O 5.0 g
Yeast extract 1.0 g
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

Adjust pH to 5.5-6.0 and autoclave. Add sodium thiosulfate after autoclaving from a sterile stock solution sterilized by filtration. Best growth is observed in the syneresis water of slant agar tubes (20.0 g/l agar).

For DSM 22701 change amount of yeast extract to 0.5 g/l and of Na-thiosulfate to 2.5 g/l.

© 2011 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


