        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, solid culture medium comprised of glucose, yeast extract, calcium carbonate, and agar.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium105.pdf

105. GLUCONOBACTER OXYDANS MEDIUM

Glucose 100.0 g
Yeast extract 10.0 g
CaCO3 20.0 g
Agar 15.0 g
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

Adjust pH to 6.8.

20 g calcium carbonate in the medium serves as a buffer. The calcium carbonate will settle in agar plates before the agar has set, producing an opaque layer in the bottom. As the strain grows and acid is produced this will react with the calcium carbonate, causing it to dissolve and form zones of clearing immediately below the colonies.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Gluconobacter oxydans medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>DSM strains:
</obo:IAO_0000232>
    </owl:Class>
    


