        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Spirochaeta aurantia medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, liquid culture medium comprised of glucose, yeast extract, trypticase (trypticase peptone) agar, and potassium phosphate.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>DSM strains:
</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium168.pdf

168. SPIROCHAETA AURANTIA MEDIUM

Solution A:
Glucose 2.0 g
Yeast extract 2.0 g
Trypticase (BBL) 5.0 g
Agar (Bacto, Difco) 10.0 g
(if necessary)
Distilled water 1000.0 ml
Adjust pH to 7.5 with KOH.

Solution B:
1 M K-phosphate-buffer, pH 7.0 10.0 ml

Sterilize part A and B separately by autoclaving at 121˚C for 15 min and combine thereafter. Final pH: 7.0 - 7.3.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
