        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Acidianus brierleyi medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:definition>A minerals-salts, liquid culture medium comprised of ammonium sulfate, potassium phosphate, magnesium sulfate, potassium chloride, calcium nitrate, yeast extract, elemental sulfur, and sulfuric acid.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium150.pdf

150. ACIDIANUS BRIERLEYI MEDIUM

(NH4)2SO4 3.00 g
K2HPO4 x 3 H2O 0.50 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.50 g
KCl 0.10 g
Ca(NO3)2 0.01 g
Yeast extract 0.20 g
Sulfur (flowers) 10.00 g
Distilled water 1000.00 ml

Adjust pH with 6 N H2SO4 to 1.5 - 2.5. Yeast extract (10% w/v in distilled water) is autoclaved separately. Sulfur is sterilized by steaming for 3 hours on each of 3 successive days.

For DSM 18786 adjust pH to 0.8.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
