        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium159.pdf

159. TREPONEMA BRYANTII MEDIUM

Rumen fluid, clarified 300.000 ml
CaCl2 x 2 H2O 0.120 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.180 g
KH2PO4 0.450 g
K2HPO4 0.450 g
NaCl 0.900 g
(NH4)2SO4 0.900 g
Resazurin 0.001 g
Cysteine-HCl x H2O 1.000 g
Distilled water 580.000 ml
Adjust pH to 7.0 with KOH
NaHCO3 solution (5% w/v) 100.000 ml
Glucose solution (10% w/v) 20.000 ml

The medium is prepared under 100% CO2 atmosphere. Sodium bicarbonate and glucose solution are filter-sterilized and added to the main part of the medium after it has been autoclaved and cooled to room temperature. Final pH should be 6.7 - 7.0.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:definition>A minerals-salts, liquid culture medium comprised of clarified rumen fluid, calcium chloride, magnesium sulfate, potassium phosphate, sodium chloride, ammonium sulfate, resazurin, cysteine hydrochloride, sodium bicarbonate, and glucose.  Prepared under an atmosphere of carbon dioxide.</obo:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


