205. NATRONOBACTERIUM MEDIUM

Casamino acids 15.0 g
Na3-citrate x 2 H2O 3.0 g
Glutamic acid 2.5 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 2.5 g
KCl 2.0 g
NaCl 250.0 g
Agar 20.0 g

Add distilled water to give a final volume of 1000.0 ml.
Dissolve agar by heating before adding sodium chloride. Adjust pH to 7.0 before autoclaving. Adjust pH to 8.5 with sterile 5% Na2CO3 after heat sterilization of the medium.

