        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, liquid culture medium comprised of sodium chloride, magnesium sulfate, potassium chloride, yeast extract, trypticase (trypticase peptone), vitamin solution, trace elements, thioglycolate, ascorbate, glucose, and sodium hydroxide.  Prepared under an atmosphere of dinitrogen.</obo:definition>
        <obo:createdBy>Carrine Blank</obo:createdBy>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Haloanaerobium medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium210.pdf

210. HALOANAEROBIUM MEDIUM

NaCl 130.0 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 8.8 g
KCl 1.0 g
Yeast extract 10.0 g
Trypticase (BBL) 10.0 g
Vitamin solution (see medium 141) 10.0 ml
Trace element solutionsee medium 144) 10.0 ml
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

Prepare the medium anaerobically under 100% N2. After autoclaving add from sterile solutions:

Thioglycolate-ascorbate reducing agent (see below) 25.0 ml
Glucose 10% (w/v) 25.0 ml
2 N NaOH 10.0 ml
Final pH: 9.0.

Thioglycolate-ascorbate solution:
Na-thioglycolate 0.5 g
Na-ascorbate 0.5 g
Distilled water 25.0 ml

Filter sterilize.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>DSM strains:
</obo:IAO_0000232>
    </owl:Class>
    


