        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, solid culture medium comprised of peptone, yeast extract, agar, and filtered aged seawater or artificial sea water.</obo:definition>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>seawater yeast peptone agar</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>DSM strains:
</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium243.pdf

243. SEAWATER YEAST PEPTONE AGAR

Peptone 5.0 g
Yeast extract 3.0 g
Agar 12.0 g
Distilled water 250.0 ml
Filtered, aged seawater 750.0 ml
(see below)

Adjust pH to 7.8. Boil for 5 min, filter and readjust the pH to 7.3.

*Natural sea water is stored in the dark for at least three weeks to &quot;age&quot;. If natural sea water is not available use artificial sea water.

Artificial sea water:
NaCl 28.13 g
KCl 0.77 g
CaCl2 x 2 H2O 1.60 g
MgCl2 x 6 H2O 4.80 g
NaHCO3 0.11 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 3.50 g
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


