        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium246.pdf

246. SEA WATER AGAR

Beef extract 10.0 g
Peptone 10.0 g
Agar 20.0 g
Tap water 250.0 ml
Sea water* 750.0 ml

Dissolve beef extract and peptone by heating in tap water, adjust pH to 7.8 and boil for 10 min. Readjust pH to 7.3. Add agar and autoclave at 121˚C for 20 min. Directly after autoclaving, add warm (55˚C) sterile sea water. Liquid medium without agar should be combined when cooled to room temperature.
*Natural sea water is stored in the dark for at least three weeks to &quot;age&quot;. If natural sea water is not available use artificial sea water.

Artificial sea water:
NaCl 28.13 g
KCl 0.77 g
CaCl2 x 2 H2O 1.60 g
MgCl2 x 6 H2O 4.80 g
NaHCO3 0.11 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 3.50 g
Distilled water

© 2008 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>sea water agar</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, solid culture medium comprised of beef extract, peptone, agar, and filtered aged sea water or artificial sea water.</obo:definition>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>DSM strains:
</obo:IAO_0000232>
    </owl:Class>
    


