        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium371.pdf

371. NATRONOBACTERIA MEDIUM

KH2PO4 1.00 g
KCl 1.00 g
NH4Cl 1.00 g
MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.24 g
CaSO4 x 2 H2O 0.17 g
Trace element solution SL-10
(see medium 320) 1.00 ml
Agar, if necessary 20.00 g
NaCl 200.00 g
Na2-glutamate 1.00 g
Yeast extract 5.00 g
Casamino acids 5.00 g
Na2CO3 5.00 g

Add distilled water to give a final volume of 1000 ml.
Adjust pH to 6.5 before autoclaving!
Sterilize Na2CO3 separate from medium, add after cooling. Check final pH to be 9.0 - 9.5.
If agar medium is prepared, heat and dissolve agar before adding sodium chloride.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
