        <obo:definition>An organic-rich, liquid culture medium comprised of trypticase peptone, casamino acids, yeast extract, glucose, monosodium glutamate, arginine, glycine, tryptopha, potassium phosphate, tween 80 (polysorbate 80), and cysteine hydrochloride.</obo:definition>
        <obo:has_exact_synonym>Acidaminococcus fermentans medium</obo:has_exact_synonym>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium414.pdf

414. ACIDAMINOCOCCUS FERMENTANS MEDIUM

Trypticase peptone 5.0 g
Casamino acids 10.0 g
Yeast extract 5.0 g
Glucose 5.0 g
Na-glutamate 4.0 g
Arginine 1.0 g
Glycine 1.0 g
DL-Tryptophan 0.1 g
KH2PO4 2.0 g
Tween 80 0.5 ml
Cysteine-HCl x H2O 0.5 g
Distilled water 1000.0 ml

pH 7.0 - 7.2.

© 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved</obo:IAO_0000119>
    </owl:Class>
    


